      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You're right that entropy wins in the end—nothing you build will last, and every story fades to static. But logic alone doesn't capture what it feels like to laugh, to love, to taste something good, or to feel the sun on your skin. Those moments don't need to be permanent to be real; they're meaningful precisely because they're fleeting. Accepting the void doesn't have to mean surrendering to it—it can mean letting go of the pressure to make everything matter, and just being here for the experience.",
